Found during k40 (posix worker): `bun test bootstrap/test` leaves ~46 getty-bun-test-* dirs per run in TMPDIR; each file alone leaves none. Likely cause: bootstrap/test/lib/harness.ts registers its afterEach on import (:156), which attaches to one file only (comment at :21 says scenarios.test.ts) - against the hazard rule that each test file cleans up in its own afterEach/afterAll. On 2026-11-26 690 leftovers (47G) filled a tmpfs /tmp and caused false failures; the main session removed them (no bun test running). Fix in the test-writer lane: each test file registers its own cleanup; a check that a full run leaves no getty-bun-test-* dir.

2026-11-26 related (windows reviewer, k40): the bootstrap harness passes XDG_CACHE_HOME (Windows: LOCALAPPDATA, TEMP) through, so a starter run in the suite can write Bun's default transpiler cache into the developer's real cache. Scope the cache dirs to the sandbox in the same fix.

